# Accessibility Standards

- Use semantic HTML whenever possible.
- Prefer semantic elements over generic div/span containers.

## Forms

- Every input must have a label.
- Associate labels correctly.
- Show accessible validation messages.

## Interaction

- All interactions must be keyboard accessible.
- Use button for actions.
- Use anchor for navigation.

## Accessibility behavior

- Preserve visible focus states.
- Do not rely only on color for meaning.
- Use aria-* only when semantic HTML is insufficient.

## Images

- All meaningful images require alt text.
- Decorative images should not pollute screen readers.

## Structure

- Use logical heading hierarchy.
- Avoid skipping heading levels unnecessarily.